  "solution": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mn>20</mn></msub><mi>Ca</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ca</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mn>8</mn></math><br /><br />Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ca</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math> electrons each in outermost and penultimate shell.",
